<div style="position: relative; z-index: 3; max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 56px)">
<div id="parents" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px; scroll-margin-top: 90px">
<h2 id="shs-parents" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 64px); line-height: 1.0; letter-spacing: 0.02em; text-wrap: balance; text-align: center; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">Are you a teacher or parent?</h2>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(380px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 20px">
<article class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(90, 30, 50, 0.55); border-radius: 26px; padding: 30px 30px 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<span style="font-family: 'Jen Wagner Print', sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 0.62; letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: uppercase; color: #9E2A17">For teachers</span>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B3552">SheHacksSwift runs in the school holidays, so students miss no class time and there’s no excursion paperwork. It’s a three-day intensive that fits alongside a school <a href="https://developer.apple.com/learn/swift-coding-club/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight: 600; color: #1B1530;">Swift Coding Club</a>, or helps start one. Our get-ready steps use Apple’s Develop in Swift tutorials, and Apple’s free <a href="https://apple.co/dis-educatorguide" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight: 600; color: #1B1530;">Educator Guide</a> walks teachers through the same tutorials.</p>
</article>
<article class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(90, 30, 50, 0.55); border-radius: 26px; padding: 30px 30px 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<span style="font-family: 'Jen Wagner Print', sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 0.62; letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: uppercase; color: #9E2A17">For parents</span>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B3552">Your child can sign up themselves. If they’re offered a place, you’ll get the consent forms to complete. Every mentor holds a Working With Children Check, and our online community is moderated by Girl Geek Academy.</p>
</article>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 20px; text-align: center">
<p style="margin: 0; max-width: 34em; font-size: clamp(18px, 1.6vw, 21px); line-height: 1.5; color: #1B1530">Share this page with the girl geeks you know. For questions, or to bring SheHacksSwift to your school or city, email <a href="mailto:hello@girlgeekacademy.com" style="color: #1B1530; font-weight: 700">hello@girlgeekacademy.com</a>.</p>
