<section id="faq" aria-labelledby="shs-faq" class="shs-g" style="position: relative; z-index: 2; background-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #d48aa6 0%, #a268c1 45%, #4b3773 100%); color: #1B1530; padding: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px) 20px clamp(56px, 6vw, 96px)"><div class="shs-swart shs-swart-faq" aria-hidden="true" style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: clamp(260px, 34vw, 500px); z-index: 1; pointer-events: none"><div class="shs-swart-img" style="width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 2362 / 582; background: url('/images/shehacksswift/swift-org/wave-swoop.png') no-repeat center / 100% 100%"></div></div>
<div style="position: relative; z-index: 3; max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 56px)">
<h2 id="shs-faq" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 64px); line-height: 1.0; letter-spacing: 0.02em; text-wrap: balance; text-align: center; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">Frequently asked questions</h2>
<div class="shs-faq" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(320px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 18px; align-items: start">
<div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">What’s Swift?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">Swift is the programming language used to create apps for Apple devices. With its clear and expressive syntax, you’ll be bringing your ideas to life in no time.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">Do I need experience with Swift or coding?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">No. Online sessions before the event and Day 1 get you started. If you already code, you can go as far as you like.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">What’s an app playground?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">A small app built in Swift Playground or Xcode that someone can explore in about three minutes. It’s the format the Swift Student Challenge asks for, so it’s what you’ll build.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">Will I finish my app in three days?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">You’ll leave with a working app playground and a plan for what to polish. You can keep improving it until the Challenge closes, with online mentors and office hours to help.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">What do I need to bring?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">One Mac or iPad, your lunch and a willingness to learn. Swift Playground runs on Mac and iPad; Xcode needs a Mac.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">Can I use AI to help me code?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">Xcode includes AI coding help. Apple’s rules for the 2026 Challenge allowed AI tools as long as you explained how you used them. We’ll go through the 2027 rules with you when they’re out.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">What are the hours?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">9:30am–4:00pm each day.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">Who can apply?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">High school girls and gender-diverse students in Australia, including non-binary students, who’ll be 13 or older by February 2027.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">What’s the Swift Student Challenge?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">Apple’s annual coding challenge for students: you build an app playground and submit it yourself. The 2027 Challenge opens in early 2027, and SheHacksSwift gets your entry started.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">Can I work with my friends?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">Yes. You’ll be in a crew of 4 to 6 for ideas, testing and demos. Swift Student Challenge entries are individual, though, so everyone builds and submits their own app playground. Mentors coach and explain. They can look things up with you, but they never type code into your project.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">Do my parents need to do anything?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">Not to sign up. You can do that yourself. If you’re offered a place, a parent or guardian completes the consent forms within 7 days to confirm it.</p>
</div><div class="shs-glass" style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -30px rgba(60, 20, 70, 0.6); border-radius: 22px; padding: 24px 26px 26px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; break-inside: avoid">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Piñata LimesSans-Black', sans-serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: #1B1530; text-transform: uppercase">What happens after January?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; color: #3B3552">We stay with you until your entry is in: online mentors, office hours and reminders when the Challenge opens.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 10px 18px"><a class="shs-btn" href={urls.sheHacksSwiftRegister} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display: inline-block; text-decoration: none; font-family: 'Jen Wagner Print', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 32px; line-height: 0.55; letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 10px 22px; border-radius: 999px; white-space: nowrap; background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, #F05138 0%, #D2342A 100%); color: #ffffff">Sign up</a><span style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; color: #E9DFFF">Takes about five minutes.</span></div>
</div>

